Please find attached weekly performance report of DME.

I. Sales & Marketing
1) Market Situation and Competiton  Activities
TPS/TAS Market volume slow down, due to forthcoming holidays in USA
With the limited volume for this trade , carriers in this market are not confident to announce rate increase
Happag, MSC are very aggressive in the market for TAS/TPS
AES     Market volume for both NWC & MED ports, are further affected, due to christmas holidays approaching in Europe
With current problems in Egypt, the market volume is drastically slowed down
Although HJS announced GRI in this market ( $ 400/T w e f 15th Dec'2013 ), no other carriers have announed in this market
IAS (Outbound)  IAS Outbound market volumes are stable
Secured new customers Syed Metal(25T/WK) & Eagle Trans (20T/WK)
Vehicle movements which is major commodity affected due to delay in 2014 model vehicle to the Far East still not started
Market volume for East Africa is stable
Carriers CMA / ESL /PIL /EMC /HMM  ave increased rates by usd 500/teu to East Africa
Maersk /SAF are not participating in this rate increase and continue to offer $ 200/TEU for this sector, Maersk got direction from the management to offer lower rates, till one of consortium pulls out of this trade
IAS ( Inbound ) Traditionally, market volume during this period is always good, but this year, market volume not improved inspite festival season ahead
Rate levels have maintained at same rate levels of $ 650/1300/1300 compared to last week
IRA 1st Dec RR $200/T, which is likely to be successful with 50%

